            <ArticleTitle>Ultrasound-Guided Removal of an Infected Loose Body from the Quadriceps Muscle.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>143</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.2484/rcr.v3i3.143</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present the case of a 35 year-old male with pain and swelling in his right thigh. By CT and sonography, an abscess was localized to the deep, anteromedial, mid-thigh within the quadriceps muscle, along with a 1.3 cm loose body. The infected loose body was removed under ultrasound guidance without complications.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
